Z||000005||bHooper||08-07-2001||01:37 PM||||Patrick,  Melinda's parents live at lake of the Ozarks.  I've been there twice.  It's like a big Smith Mountain Lake.<P>They currently own a resort <A HREF="http://bayhillyunkers.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://bayhillyunkers.com/</A>   <P>They currently have it up for sale, but if they still have it next year, we should get a learge group together and head out there for the show!<P>Of course, I may be driveing the fiero by myself, while Melinda fly's out.  She wasn't to thrilled with the comfort afforded one in a fiero, for 5 hours   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>From Greensboro, it is approximatly 1000 miles to lake of the Ozarks.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||08-07-2001||06:41 PM||||Lake of the Ozarks? Thats in Branson,MO...EEK!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I lived there for about a year a couple of years ago....all I can say, again, is <B><FONT SIZE="3">EEK!!!</B></FONT><BR>Think I'll skip that one. No offense to anyone who lives there, but I used to live there so I can bash it lol. If its in the summer, get ready for some overheating cars! Only way through that town is on 76 Country Blvd..(the strip, as its called there)..Its TWO lanes, UP and DOWN, UP and DOWN. Traffic is always at a dead stand still, and you'll be stuck behind 90 year old tourists in their Winnabegos (sp).....Like I said, I lived there..just warning ya! Have fun!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Edit..ok on a good note, it IS a beautiful place.......there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000007||Cheever2||08-07-2001||06:50 PM||||I'm hoping it will be at Osage Beach, which is 129 miles north of Branson.  I have sent to Gloria my suggestion to have it here: <A HREF="http://www.tan-tar-a.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tan-tar-a.com</A>  <BR>It's pricey but there are surely more affordable places nearby.<P>I asked her about the dates.  No reply yet.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rob Durham||08-07-2001||07:53 PM||||Branson would be alot better than Osage Beach, nicer and cheaper places to stay ALOT more to do and with the strip being wider now trafic isn't near as bad as it use to be, I have been here for the last 7 years and there have been major ghanges in the last 2 years.<P>You wont overheat any more in Branson than you will in Osage Beach.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://rs-designs.com/87GT.html" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://rs-designs.com/Banner.jpg">  </A>||||reg||10
